/> If that's not enough you can make the roll harder, or have it be the lair of some sort of 'lacking' spirit or sloth spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-10-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:05:12-07:00","id":985020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>salientmind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/984988-do-shoals-seem-weak-to-anyone-else#post984988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fluff is terrifying, but I play with former D&amp;D players. So I can write an awesome description, and the reaction to the negative is &quot;whatever. We can pull it off&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It does seem weak, and not accurate as well since it doesn't measure length of exposure only number of attempts to leave. I would add this to the formula:<br /> <br /> Each Scene within a particular Shoal requires the aforementioned Resolve + Composure Roll to avoid accumulating the penalty, and penalties accumulated in that particular Shoal by failures are not cleared by success in leaving. These penalties may only be reduced back down to zero by performing cleansing (washing, grooming, bathing, ect..) actions within a Glade. Such a cleaning actions reduces the penalties accumulated in all Shoals to zero.<br /> <br /> This also makes Glades extremely valuable territories to hold. Two birds with one stone.<br /> <br /> Also harder penalties are less intimidating than lingering penalties, which mark the character as somehow tainted and fixing it is now contingent on access to a limited resource they may or may not control (bonus Controlling a Glade is now a Treasure you can reward your players with, with the twist of then needing to defend it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-11-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}